{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1294878-hyperbolic-time-chambers","id":1294878,"title":"Hyperbolic Time Chambers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-07T14:03:58-08:00","id":1294878,"title":"Hyperbolic Time Chambers?","content":"I've been thinking. If someone created a <a href=\"https://dragonball.fandom.com/wiki/Hyperbolic_Time_Chamber\" target=\"_blank\">Hyperbolic Time Chamber</a> (where time moves much faster in the chamber) than without, how would training in there incur paradox or not? The assumption is that one would use such a vulgar device in a sanctum, Realm, or the Umbra.<br /> <br /> The basic effect is Time 3. Maybe higher because effecting an area and not just one person?<br /> <br /> If, say, someone adds a life 4 effect that causes aging at an inverted rate so to an outside observer, the person ages normally. (i.e. Chamber is 10x faster than normal, but people age at 1/10 the rate). Would this cause paradox?<br /> <br /> If someone stays in and doesn't age, but trains alot and raises their dots more than &quot;normal&quot;... would the person using higher skills, whether magical or mundane, suffer paradox?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","user":"Tytalus","date":". 03-08-2019, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T15:39:16-08:00","id":1294904,"title":"","content":"When you leave the Time chamber you would likely incur Paradox in a similar fashion to the specialist bred / modified power armour pilots tend to when they come back to earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T18:31:35-08:00","id":1294942,"title":"","content":"It Depends honestly how blatant you are about it.. like go into a room and come out tomorrow with a years worth of training.. Paradox. If maybe you have a couple days worth it just seems &quot;Efficient&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T03:17:17-08:00","id":1295002,"title":"","content":"It really depends: What is the observer-related &quot;this can't be possible / This should not exist&quot;?<br /> <br /> If they look the same when leaving the chamber (No sudden muscle mass growth, no obvious sudden aging, etc.), then I don't see Paradox suddenly striking. To an observer, nothing is wrong (TM). They just entered a chamber and left a couple days later. Nothing to see here, move along.<br /> <br /> Just because you suddenly have more knowledge and/or muscle memory, does not mean that suddenly Paradox will strike. It is as 'subtle' as you suddenly gaining knowledge of a faraway place through scrying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 03-08-2019, 06:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T09:45:03-08:00","id":1295071,"title":"","content":"Most Time 3 effects tend to be vulgar by default and messing with them can cause Pattern Bleed<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T09:58:00-08:00","id":1295072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1294878-hyperbolic-time-chambers?p=1295071#post1295071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most Time 3 effects tend to be vulgar by default and messing with them can cause Pattern Bleed</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point, the assumption is that one would use a Hyperbolic Time Chamber in a Sanctum, a Realm, or the Umbra.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1294878-hyperbolic-time-chambers?p=1294942#post1294942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It Depends honestly how blatant you are about it.. like go into a room and come out tomorrow with a years worth of training.. Paradox. If maybe you have a couple days worth it just seems &quot;Efficient&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, I can see a year:day hyperbolic time chamber causing problems. (Also, it would require 730 successes to pull off, so such a huge ratio likely doesn't exist anyways.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1294878-hyperbolic-time-chambers?p=1295002#post1295002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really depends: What is the observer-related &quot;this can't be possible / This should not exist&quot;?<br /> <br /> If they look the same when leaving the chamber (No sudden muscle mass growth, no obvious sudden aging, etc.), then I don't see Paradox suddenly striking. To an observer, nothing is wrong (TM). They just entered a chamber and left a couple days later. Nothing to see here, move along.<br /> <br /> Just because you suddenly have more knowledge and/or muscle memory, does not mean that suddenly Paradox will strike. It is as 'subtle' as you suddenly gaining knowledge of a faraway place through scrying.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense. What I'm curious about is heavy sustained use of them over time. So, say someone has a chamber with 5days per day ratio. Say they live in there the bulk of their time for a couple months. They'll have 8 extra months experience/knowledge. That will probably pass the smell test. But.. Then they do this for <b>two years</b>. Now they have 8 extra years worth of experience/knowledge. Maybe knowledge of more spheres than normal too.<br /> <br /> Would using advanced spheres cause paradox? Would having mastery (5 dots) in several abilities cause paradox now? Or high attributes?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T11:24:03-08:00","id":1295090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1294878-hyperbolic-time-chambers?p=1295072#post1295072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They'll have 8 extra months experience/knowledge. That will probably pass the smell test. But.. Then they do this for <b>two years</b>. Now they have 8 extra years worth of experience/knowledge. Maybe knowledge of more spheres than normal too.<br /> <br /> Would using advanced spheres cause paradox? Would having mastery (5 dots) in several abilities cause paradox now? Or high attributes?</div> </div> </div> </div>This...really is one of the things the ST needs to decide. Generally, it is unclear how long the 'memory' of the theoretical observer would be. Personally I usually take the approach of the observer having quite a short term memory - it's more of an 'in the moment' thing than anything else, as well as it depending on the blunt blatantness of the effect or visual change. So I personally would rule that, no, no paradox is involved if they just step out and make use of their abilities a while later. Which is different than them stepping out and suddenly looking ripped and old.<br /> <br /> Now, one could say 'Woo, that's quite a thing to exploit! Let's make time chambers and train five times faster!'. But: There is also the human element. Spending a year semi-alone inside the same chamber? No contact with others? Your natural timespan shortened by 5 years instead of 1 to the outside world? Not seeking the knowledge and wisdom of *others* for that whole year?<br /> <br /> Unless you make the time chamber your literal home that you share with friends and/or a loved one (who then *also* need to be okay with not meeting their other friends...), it'd sound hellish to me.<br /> Oh, of course your friends could leave the chamber to get things, meet people and come back later...but for every hour they are gone, they are going to miss five whole hours in there...and if *you* are in trouble in there, don't expect help to arrive on time, ever.<br /> <br /> Abusing the powers of magick methods comes easy, but the social and mental consequences aren't always as simple <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T00:40:29-08:00","id":1295521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1294878-hyperbolic-time-chambers?p=1295072#post1295072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good point, the assumption is that one would use a Hyperbolic Time Chamber in a Sanctum, a Realm, or the Umbra.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Right, I can see a year:day hyperbolic time chamber causing problems. (Also, it would require 730 successes to pull off, so such a huge ratio likely doesn't exist anyways.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That makes sense. What I'm curious about is heavy sustained use of them over time. So, say someone has a chamber with 5days per day ratio. Say they live in there the bulk of their time for a couple months. They'll have 8 extra months experience/knowledge. That will probably pass the smell test. But.. Then they do this for <b>two years</b>. Now they have 8 extra years worth of experience/knowledge. Maybe knowledge of more spheres than normal too.<br /> <br /> Would using advanced spheres cause paradox? Would having mastery (5 dots) in several abilities cause paradox now? Or high attributes?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Issue Is less a matter of dots on a sheet and more a matter of not allowing things to decompress. If you are spending all your time in the hyperbolic time chamber with a 1/5 ratio. It is going to catch up to you. I mean there are rotes to speed up learning and teaching.. there's a reason people don't use them all the time every time. You need time to integrate them and you need time to integrate with the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}